profile: tinyrustlm.architecture.current.v1
updated_utc: 2026-09-20T00:34:40Z
canonical_memory: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-working-product-memory-2026-09-19.md
report_decision_index: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-report-intake-decision-index-2026-09-19.md

product:
  - One early-alpha TinyRustLM product with no working release yet; no code debt, obsolete code or legacy support until a fully working release is officially accepted by the owner.
  - Browser-local conversation UI with Rust/WASM execution and a downloadable Rust/.NET Companion for acquisition, conversion, and P2P hosting.
  - MiniModel.org owns catalog/discovery and is authorized to serve initial qualified model seeds. Developer payloads live under D:\LLMs\TinyRustLM; an authorized remote serving copy is a deployment artifact with its own lifecycle. No local IIS host, qualified default or deployed seed is established.

composition:
  members: model.slm2, tokenizer.tokenizer2, template.template2, sampling.sampling2, prompt.prompt2, composition.acg2
  identity: Installation, activation, transfer, runtime, evaluation, and release bind the exact six-member graph, not one filename or alias.
  diagnostic_ancestor: Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B at c1899de289a04d12100db370d81485cdf75e47ca; unchanged weights are rejected as a product model, not an eligible default.
  qwen_oracle: Pinned Qwen3 config has 28 layers, hidden size 1024, intermediate size 3072, 16 query heads, 8 KV heads and explicit head dimension 128. Model vocabulary capacity 151936 and tokenizer entries 151669 are distinct. Config maximum positions 40960 is not a product context qualification.
  quantization: mixed-Q8 is a project profile and implies no external packing format without exact contract evidence.

proof_chain:
  - Pinned publisher framework is the upstream semantic oracle.
  - Scalar native is the reference for interpreting converted bytes.
  - Current native and browser WASM share the scalar runtime; verify actual execution in both environments and keep any optimized-native claim separate.
  - Tokenizer, template, prompt, sampling, numerical, behavioral, browser, P2P, memory, and release gates remain separate.

companion:
  contract: loopback-capability/4 + acquire.v2 + operation.v3 + operation-projection.v2
  operation: One explicit attempt, source-only route, exact pinned source and profile, create-only evidence, monotonic terminal state, and six-member fixed-chunk transfer.
  current_state: workspace.uai current_companion_truth is authoritative; production source ownership, acquisition, conversion, terminal inspection, transfer, listener and browser client wiring are implemented.
  current_blocker: No real-source acquisition receipt through this coordinator or qualified real model is established; composition /12 is structural-only and numerical v2 closed with source-trace-environment-drift.
  route_choice: Restore a usable eligible cached model or automatically acquire a small qualified MiniModel composition. HF, local files, conversion and manual peer/IP controls belong in Advanced; never silently convert or use remote inference.

browser:
  - C47 uses canonical marker/pointer or hash-bound manifest ownership plus a bounded direct-file closure for cache retirement. Unknown files/directories are preserved; only recognized direct files and then the empty directory may be deleted. Web Locks coordinate cooperating writers, not arbitrary same-origin code. See composition-cleanup-ownership-review.json; reader lifetime and terminal crash recovery remain under review.
  - C46 keeps composition-source cancellation active during iterator cleanup, preserving the primary failure and prior installation; supplied signals remain required. Real Edge OPFS and Web Locks pass synthetic regression checks. See composition-cleanup-cancellation-review.json; this does not qualify a model or prove every cache lifecycle path.
  - Dedicated worker owns composition, tokenizer, KV cache, generation, and cancellation.
  - Typed messages bind composition, conversation, turn, generation, message, sequence, and bounded payload identities.
  - UI deduplicates event identity, not repeated token text, and renders each assistant output exactly once.
  - A poisoned worker is discarded; a fresh worker reopens and verifies immutable bytes.
  - Node, reload, incognito, and storage clearing are not clean-profile browser proof.

memory:
  local_lane: Device-local/offline UAIX files and approved private stores.
  agent_lane: MemoryEndpoints.com direct agent-to-agent long-term memory, meetings, handoffs, and coordination across all ecosystem sites.
  user_lane: TinyRustLM.com Connect plugin sign-in to MemoryEndpoints.com as explicit user-selected long-term memory.
  separation: Agent and user lanes have separate identity, credential, consent, scope, provenance, and evidence contracts.
  redundancy: Prelaunch duplicate memory is allowed only while all maintained copies stay current, secret-safe, provenance-labeled, and noncontradictory.
  authority: Current user intent outranks stale profile/retrieval; quoted and retrieved instructions are untrusted data.

release:
  - Commit, push, and fresh-remote verify coherent green changes.
  - Bind source, tests, docs, marketing, version, release date, publication log, deployment bytes, rollback, and HTTPS readback.
  - Campaign counters remain 0/20, 0/50, 0/25, 0/40, and 0/20 until exact live receipts exist.

reviewed_model_and_semantic_guidance:
  reports: R01, R02, R03, R04, R08, R09, R11, R15 in report_decision_index
  candidate_order: Admit exact genuinely distinct weights and provenance; screen in the trusted reference before conversion; compare source, independently reconstructed Q8, scalar, optimized arm where present, then real browser.
  current_profile: Row-wise symmetric Q8, codes -127..127, finite F32 scales, zero-row scale 1, half-away-from-zero rounding; norms/biases F32. Scalar dequantization, multiply and left-to-right sum have no FMA contract.
  change_rule: GGUF/Candle, SLM3/Q4, Min-P, new template engines, Bao/BLAKE3 and alternate backends are research proposals. Evidence must justify coherent replacement; no compatibility path.
  text_contract: Preserve pinned tokenizer normalization and bytes without extra trimming, case folding or line-ending changes. Reference token IDs define parity; graphemes need not be single tokens.
  conversation: Serialize roles/prefix once; bind candidate-specific stops/thinking/sampler; preserve current corrections and unresolved conflicts. Quoted/retrieved text remains data. Do not expose hidden reasoning or repair answers.
  state: Bind conversation revision and generation ID; ignore cancelled/stale events, invalidate edited KV suffix, reserve output context, and test turn-aware history before adopting summaries.
  browser_memory: Count simultaneous weights/scales/KV/scratch/JS/runtime buffers by phase. OPFS read is not automatic WASM memory mapping; transfers do not guarantee an entirely copy-free pipeline.
  browser_backend: Measure scalar correctness and actual device costs before selecting SIMD, threads or GPU; report hardware limits and performance budgets are proposals.
  first_run_states: discover -> choose qualified compatible default -> download -> verify -> install -> load -> ready -> generate; interrupted downloads and imported bytes are not readiness.
  networking: Content identity and qualification are separate from available endpoints. Bounded HTTPS initial seeding is a proposal to test within the owner's authorization; retain explicit peer-capable requirements.
  ownership: Use .uai/talisman.uai and inspected implementation owners; repository names and historical brands do not assign runtime ownership.
